    "overviewDetail": "Singapore is one of the worldΓÇÖs most advanced and business-friendly economies, consistently ranked among the top jurisdictions for ease of doing business, transparency, and regulatory efficiency. Strategically located in Southeast Asia, it serves as a gateway to the ASEAN market and a hub for global trade, finance, and technology.\n\nThe country offers a robust legal framework based on English common law, strong intellectual property protection, and a highly efficient digital governance system. Businesses can be incorporated quickly through the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority (ACRA), often within a day. Singapore allows 100% foreign ownership, with minimal capital requirements and a straightforward compliance structure.\n\nIts competitive tax regime includes a headline corporate tax rate of 17%, along with various exemptions and incentives for startups and SMEs. There is no capital gains tax, and the country has an extensive network of double taxation treaties, making it highly attractive for international structuring.\n\nWith world-class infrastructure, political stability, and a highly skilled workforce, Singapore continues to attract startups, multinational corporations, and investors seeking a reliable and scalable business environment.\n",
